      <pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:05:48 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Most buyers pay too much for takeovers, so says the common wisdom. But sometimes the alternative to paying up is to watch your business stagnate. Facing this dilemma, French drugmaker Sanofi SA has chosen a $41 billion US biotech acquisition as the lesser evil. It’s the right decision, and looks like a rare piece of elegant dealmaking from Europe into the US.</description>
